4417: \subsection{Review-bundle and archive-equivalence condition}
4418: 
4419: The archive-equivalence material in this subsection is deliberately bounded to
4420: this package: it only decides when the finite review-bundle records cited above
4421: are available to reviewers.  A general calculus of support-surface replacement,
4422: archive locators, and digest-preserving mirrors is a split-candidate
4423: infrastructure note rather than an additional theorem package for the present
4424: CICM presentation route.
4425: 
4426: \begin{table}
4427: \caption{Finite archive-equivalence criterion for replacing the review bundle.}
4428: \label{tab:review-bundle-archive-equivalence}
4429: \scriptsize
4430: \begin{tabularx}{\linewidth}{p{0.25\linewidth}X p{0.25\linewidth}}
4431: \toprule
4432: Criterion & Required data in the archive replacement & Failure effect \\
4433: \midrule
4434: Manifest identity & a root record byte-identical to \path{review_bundle/REVIEW_BUNDLE_MANIFEST.json}, except for an added archive URL or DOI field that is not used by the verifier & replacement rejected \\
4435: Bundle version & the identity tuple \path{(supplemental_review_bundle, 2026-06-01, 3fb3d6a0641767388a401883062aa522ea0b397b)} from the manifest fields \path{bundle_kind}, \path{created}, and \path{public_interface.public_source_commit} & replacement rejected \\
4436: Finite file list & exactly the regular files named by the manifest, submission-interface map, source-snapshot record, case-snapshot rows, verifier-script fields, and verifier-log fields; generated cache files such as \path{__pycache__/} are excluded & replacement rejected \\
4437: Content hashes & a SHA-256 digest for each file in that finite file list, equal to the digest of the corresponding file in the submitted \path{review_bundle/} at final packaging time & replacement rejected \\
4438: Path semantics & every path in the archive preserves the same relative name below \path{review_bundle/} and no certificate row is retargeted to a different file & replacement rejected \\
4439: \bottomrule
4440: \end{tabularx}
4441: \end{table}
4442: 
4443: \begin{auditrecord}[Review-bundle archive-equivalence criterion]
4444: \label{audit:review-bundle-archive-equivalence}
4445: An archival replacement for \path{review_bundle/} is accepted by this manuscript
4446: only if it satisfies all rows of
4447: Table~\ref{tab:review-bundle-archive-equivalence}.  Equivalently, it must have
4448: the same manifest identity, the same bundle-version tuple, the same finite
4449: certificate file list, the same SHA-256 content digests at final packaging time,
4450: and the same relative path semantics as the submitted \path{review_bundle/}.
4451: If no such hash-and-manifest archive is supplied, the only accepted support
4452: surface is the exact \path{review_bundle/} directory uploaded with the
4453: submission.
4454: \medskip
4455: \noindent\emph{Verification.} The manifest identity criterion fixes the root record that all bundle-dependent
4456: claims cite: \path{review_bundle/REVIEW_BUNDLE_MANIFEST.json}.  Allowing only an
4457: additional archive locator field prevents the archive from silently changing the
4458: certificate schema, pass-record ledger, submission-interface map,
4459: primary-claim inventory, verifier scripts, verifier logs, pinned-source
4460: snapshot, case-evidence rows, or submission-artifact declaration.  The bundle
4461: version is finite because the current manifest carries the three displayed
4462: fields \path{bundle_kind}, \path{created}, and
4463: \path{public_interface.public_source_commit}; equality of the tuple rules out
4464: substituting a different support bundle or a different pinned source commit.
4465: 
4466: The finite file-list criterion is obtained by following only the manifest and
4467: the machine-readable interface records already used in the proofs: certificate
4468: schema, current pass records, primary-claim inventory, submission-interface map,
4469: verifier scripts and logs, source snapshot, and the case snapshots named in the
4470: case-evidence rows.  This traversal is finite because each record is a finite
4471: JSON or manuscript table row and because generated interpreter caches are not
4472: certificate surfaces.  The content-hash criterion then gives a byte-level test
4473: for every file on that finite list.  If a file is omitted, added as a replacement
4474: for a named certificate surface, or changed bytewise, either the file-list row or
4475: the SHA-256 row fails.  The path-semantics row prevents a hash-correct file from
4476: being moved under a new relative name that would make manuscript paths point to a
4477: different object.
4478: 
4479: When all five rows pass, every path used by a bundle-dependent theorem,
4480: proposition, table row, verifier record, or manifest row denotes the same bytes
4481: under the same relative name and under the same root manifest identity as in the
4482: submitted \path{review_bundle/}.  Thus the archive is equivalent for exactly the
4483: finite certificate checks made in this paper.  When any row fails, a reviewer has
4484: a finite bad subrecord: the changed manifest identity, changed version tuple,
4485: file-list discrepancy, hash mismatch, or path-retargeting witness.  In that case
4486: the archive is not accepted, and the support surface must be exact inclusion of
4487: \path{review_bundle/} in the completed submission.
4488: \end{auditrecord}
4489: 
