4572: \begin{theorem}[Exact-inclusion support-surface realization]
4573: \label{thm:exact-inclusion-support-surface-realization}
4574: For the current package the selected support branch is exact supplemental inclusion of \path{review_bundle/}, but this branch remains conditional until an external upload-or-archive instantiation record exists.  If the completed submission contains that directory with the certificate-file digests listed in
4575: \path{review_bundle/FINAL_DIGESTS_SHA256.md}, then every bundle-backed claim in
4576: this supplement has a submitted finite support surface at its stated
4577: path-verified evidence level.  If the exact directory is not submitted, then the
4578: same support conclusion holds only after replacing it by an archive satisfying
4579: the five tests of Table~\ref{tab:review-bundle-archive-equivalence}; no venue upload receipt, public DOI, or archive locator is claimed for the present package.
4580: \end{theorem}
4581: 
4582: \begin{proof}
4583: The exact-inclusion hypothesis supplies the directory named in every bundle-local
4584: path and the final digest manifest named in
4585: Audit record~\ref{prop:exact-review-bundle-upload-witness}.  By that proposition,
4586: the manifest traverses the finite certificate surfaces used by the supplement:
4587: the bundle manifest, schema, current pass-record ledger, source-interface map,
4588: primary-claim inventory, verifier scripts, verifier logs, source snapshot, and
4589: case snapshots.  Matching the listed SHA-256 digests fixes the bytes of each of
4590: those certificate files at final packaging time, while preserving the relative
4591: path names by which the manuscript refers to them.  Thus every bundle-backed
4592: claim has the submitted finite evidence surface asserted for it, and the evidence
4593: level remains path-verified because the argument checks file presence and digest
4594: identity rather than rerunning Lean, daemons, or external artifacts.
4595: 
4596: If the exact directory is absent, the proof of
4597: Audit record~\ref{audit:review-bundle-archive-equivalence} shows that the only
4598: finite replacement accepted by this paper is an archive with the same manifest
4599: identity, bundle-version tuple, finite certificate file list, per-file SHA-256
4600: digests, and relative path semantics.  Those are exactly the five tests in
4601: Table~\ref{tab:review-bundle-archive-equivalence}.  Without such an archive, at
4602: least one bundle-local path or digest row has no submitted representative, so the
4603: corresponding bundle-backed claim lacks its evidence surface.  The statement that
4604: no public DOI or archive locator is claimed is the support-mode selection in
4605: Audit record~\ref{prop:exact-review-bundle-upload-witness}; it records that this
4606: package takes the first admissible case, not the archive-equivalent case.
4607: \end{proof}
4608: 
4609: \begin{theorem}[Final support-surface closure]
4610: \label{thm:final-support-surface-closure}
4611: For the current package, using
4612: Proposition~\ref{prop:final-package-shape-convention},
4613: Audit record~\ref{prop:exact-review-bundle-upload-witness}, and
4614: Theorem~\ref{thm:exact-inclusion-support-surface-realization}, the bundle-backed
4615: claims in this supplement are admissible at the stated path-verified evidence
4616: level exactly when the submitted supplemental material contains the exact
4617: directory \path{review_bundle/} whose final packaging record is
4618: \path{review_bundle/FINAL_DIGESTS_SHA256.md}.  The exact directory branch also
4619: requires that any post-generation change to a named bundle file be followed by
4620: refreshed SHA-256 rows in that final digest record and by rerunning the finite
4621: verifiers whose records cite the changed coordinate.  A replacement archive is not a
4622: current package branch; it would have to satisfy
4623: Table~\ref{tab:review-bundle-archive-equivalence} and provide a locator before a
4624: future package could select it.  If the exact directory is not present in the
4625: current package submission, the bundle-backed claims are not part of the accepted
4626: support surface, although the short presentation artifact may still cite the
4627: pinned public \path{newmath} repository for the imported source spine.
4628: \end{theorem}
4629: 
4630: \begin{proof}
4631: Let $B$ denote the set of bundle-dependent claims in this supplement.  By the
4632: definition of \path{review_bundle/} in the problem statement and by the bundle
4633: rows of Table~\ref{tab:review-bundle-archive-equivalence}, every claim in $B$
4634: uses at least one named certificate surface under \path{review_bundle/}: the
4635: manifest, certificate schema, pass-record ledger, source-interface map,
4636: primary-claim inventory, verifier scripts or logs, the pinned source snapshot,
4637: or one of the case snapshots.  Therefore a submitted support surface for $B$
4638: must either contain those named files with their relative path semantics or
4639: replace them by an archive that is finite-file-list and hash equivalent.
4640: 
4641: If the exact directory \path{review_bundle/} is uploaded, then
4642: Audit record~\ref{prop:exact-review-bundle-upload-witness} identifies it as the
4643: current concrete support witness and all named bundle paths are present in the submitted supplemental boundary.  The file
4644: \path{review_bundle/FINAL_DIGESTS_SHA256.md} records the final SHA-256 digest
4645: surface for those certificate files, so the byte identity of the supplied
4646: directory is checkable without changing the role of the directory into an
4647: archive claim.  If a named bundle file is regenerated after that digest surface
4648: is written, the byte-coordinate selected by the support relation changes; by
4649: Proposition~\ref{prop:regenerated-theorem-inventory-digest-closure} and the same
4650: finite-coordinate argument, the corresponding digest row and verifier logs must
4651: be refreshed before the regenerated file can be the submitted support witness.
4652: Hence all claims in $B$ have the path-verified support surface asserted for this
4653: package exactly in the exact-upload-with-current-digests branch.
4654: 
4655: The archive criterion remains a finite non-current rejection test.  If a later
4656: package attempted to replace the directory by an archive, Audit
4657: record~\ref{audit:review-bundle-archive-equivalence} would require equality of
4658: the manifest identity, bundle-version tuple, finite certificate file list,
4659: per-file SHA-256 digests, and relative path semantics.  The current package does
4660: not contain the locator or archive digest table needed to enter that branch, so
4661: the theorem cannot treat an archive as an accepted present support surface.
4662: 
4663: Conversely, suppose the exact directory is not submitted for the current package.
4664: Then at least one named bundle certificate surface is outside the submitted
4665: artifact boundary and has no selected finite replacement.  The finite certificate
4666: schema used in Theorem~\ref{thm:current-package-certificate-exactness}
4667: accepts only submitted paths, explicit historical path records, and the stated
4668: supplemental surfaces.  Hence the missing bundle surface cannot support the
4669: corresponding claim in $B$.  The public \path{newmath} repository citation is a
4670: separate pinned-source citation, so it remains available for the short
4671: architectural note but does not reconstitute the omitted bundle-backed
4672: certificate records.  This proves both admissible cases and the failure of all
4673: other cases.
4674: \end{proof}
