4727: \begin{theorem}[Workspace-to-final-package reconciliation]
4728: \label{thm:workspace-final-package-reconciliation}
4729: Let $H_0$ be the automath commit
4730: \path{305ee93353b16babc461bfad1a7aee9c808ee268}, and let $D_0$ be the digest
4731: manifest \path{review_bundle/FINAL_DIGESTS_SHA256.md}.  The source-state claim
4732: made in Audit record~\ref{prop:final-immutable-package-state-certificate} is the
4733: finite package claim $(H_0,D_0)$, not a claim that every later reviewer checkout,
4734: editor workspace, or post-packaging working tree has Git \path{HEAD} equal to $H_0$.  If a
4735: current workspace reports a different Git \path{HEAD}, then the verifier-log and
4736: bundle-backed claims of this supplement remain admissible exactly in the
4737: following two reconciled cases:
4738: \begin{enumerate}
4739: \item the submitted support surface is exact inclusion of \path{review_bundle/}, or
4740: an archive equivalent to it, whose finite certificate files match the SHA-256
4741: rows of $D_0$; or
4742: \item the package is deliberately advanced to the current workspace state by
4743: rerunning the three verifier commands and replacing the displayed source-state
4744: record, the verifier logs, and the digest manifest by a new common
4745: commit--manifest certificate.
4746: \end{enumerate}
4747: In all other cases a mismatch between a later workspace \path{HEAD} and $H_0$
4748: does not certify a new package state and does not invalidate the historical
4749: finite package claim $(H_0,D_0)$; it only shows that the later workspace is
4750: outside the submitted support surface.
4751: \end{theorem}
4752: 
4753: \begin{proof}
4754: The accepted command-result coordinates are finite.  By
4755: Audit record~\ref{prop:final-immutable-package-state-certificate}, the three log
4756: paths, the displayed commit $H_0$, and the manifest $D_0$ form the source-state
4757: record for the fresh verifier runs.  By
4758: Theorem~\ref{thm:final-support-surface-closure}, those log claims are part of the
4759: accepted support surface only when the exact bundle is submitted or when an
4760: archive supplies the same finite file list, digests, and relative path semantics.
4761: Thus case (1) fixes the bytes of the certificate files directly: the reviewer's
4762: ambient checkout may have any Git \path{HEAD}, but the submitted certificate
4763: surface is still the byte-identified finite package $(H_0,D_0)$.
4764: 
4765: Suppose instead that the authors want the later workspace itself to be the
4766: package state.  Then at least one source-state coordinate has changed, namely
4767: the Git \path{HEAD} coordinate.  The verification rule in the scope contract
4768: requires every command-result claim to record its exact command, source commit,
4769: environment, exit code, and log path.  Therefore a new workspace state cannot be
4770: accepted by merely observing the new \path{HEAD}; the three verifier runs must be
4771: rerun against that state, and their logs and digest manifest must be replaced by
4772: a single consistent commit--manifest record.  This is case (2).
4773: 
4774: If neither case holds, the later workspace contributes no finite coordinate to
4775: the submitted certificate.  It is not named in $D_0$, it is not an
4776: archive-equivalent representative under Table~\ref{tab:review-bundle-archive-equivalence},
4777: and it is not accompanied by fresh verifier logs satisfying the command-result
4778: record rule.  The finite-coordinate determination boundary of
4779: Theorem~\ref{thm:finite-coordinate-determination-boundary} then forbids silently
4780: using that workspace either to certify a new package or to refute the old
4781: byte-identified package.  The only certified statement left is the historical
4782: finite package claim $(H_0,D_0)$, conditional on the exact support-surface branch
4783: already proved above.\end{proof}
4784: 
4785: \begin{auditrecord}[Mutable-checkout observations are non-certifying]
4786: \label{prop:mutable-checkout-observation-boundary}
4787: Let $W$ be a review-time working tree whose Git \path{HEAD} is not the commit
4788: $H_0$ named in Theorem~\ref{thm:workspace-final-package-reconciliation}.  The
4789: observation of $W$ is not a certificate coordinate for any verifier-log claim in
4790: this package unless $W$ is promoted by the second branch of that theorem, namely
4791: by rerunning the three verifier commands and replacing the commit, log, and digest
4792: records by a new common finite package certificate.  Consequently, a reviewer who
4793: sees $W$ with a different \path{HEAD} has exactly one source-level reconciliation
4794: test for the existing package: inspect the exact-bundle or archive-equivalent
4795: surface whose certificate-file bytes match \path{review_bundle/FINAL_DIGESTS_SHA256.md}.
4796: \medskip
4797: \noindent\emph{Verification.} The finite package certificate records three kinds of coordinates relevant here:
4798: the displayed commit, the verifier logs, and the per-file digest manifest.  A
4799: bare working-tree observation supplies none of the last two coordinates and, when
4800: its \path{HEAD} differs from $H_0$, supplies a different first coordinate.  By the
4801: command-result rule used in
4802: Audit record~\ref{prop:final-immutable-package-state-certificate}, changing a
4803: source-state coordinate requires fresh logs with their command, environment, exit
4804: code, and log path; this is precisely the promotion branch in
4805: Theorem~\ref{thm:workspace-final-package-reconciliation}.  If that branch is not
4806: performed, the observation of $W$ remains outside the finite package.  The only
4807: remaining reconciliation route is therefore the branch that checks the already
4808: selected support surface: the exact included \path{review_bundle/} directory, or
4809: an archive equivalent under Table~\ref{tab:review-bundle-archive-equivalence},
4810: with certificate bytes fixed by the final digest manifest.
4811: \end{auditrecord}
4812: 
4813: \begin{theorem}[Support-surface normal form for bundle-backed claims]
4814: \label{thm:support-surface-normal-form}
4815: For the current presentation package, every accepted use of a bundle-backed
4816: certificate coordinate is in exactly one of the following normal forms.
4817: \begin{enumerate}
4818: \item \emph{Exact inclusion}: an external upload or submission receipt records
4819: that the submitted support surface contains the exact \path{review_bundle/}
4820: directory whose certificate-file bytes match
4821: \path{review_bundle/FINAL_DIGESTS_SHA256.md}.
4822: \item \emph{Archive-equivalent inclusion}: a replacement archive satisfies every
4823: row of Table~\ref{tab:review-bundle-archive-equivalence}, including manifest
4824: identity, bundle-version identity, finite file-list identity, SHA-256 content
4825: identity, and relative path semantics.
4826: \item \emph{Promoted rerun}: the package is advanced to a new source state by
4827: rerunning the verifier commands and replacing the displayed source-state record,
4828: verifier logs, and digest manifest by one common finite commit--manifest
4829: certificate.
4830: \end{enumerate}
4831: If none of these three normal forms is present, the attempted bundle-backed
4832: reading has a finite obstruction subrecord: either the external exact-inclusion
4833: receipt is absent, the archive-equivalence table has a failed row, or the rerun
4834: branch lacks the command, source-state, environment, exit-code, log-path, and
4835: digest coordinates required by the command-boundary rule.  Thus the late
4836: support-surface chain is a finite audit-interface classification for this
4837: package, not a theorem about general archive infrastructure, venue upload, or
4838: semantic correctness of the bundled artifacts.
4839: \end{theorem}
4840: 
4841: \begin{proof}
4842: The candidate support surface for a bundle-backed coordinate can differ from the
4843: source-level package in only three record-visible ways.  First, it can supply an
4844: external receipt for the same directory selected by
4845: Proposition~\ref{prop:final-package-shape-convention}.
4846: Theorem~\ref{thm:exact-inclusion-support-surface-realization} and
4847: Theorem~\ref{thm:final-support-surface-closure} prove that this exact directory,
4848: with the final digest manifest, is the local byte surface that must be supplied;
4849: the additional receipt is what turns that local selection into submitted support.
4850: This is normal form~(1).
4851: 
4852: Second, the candidate can replace the directory by an archive.  The manuscript
4853: does not accept arbitrary archive availability as a certificate coordinate:
4854: Audit record~\ref{audit:review-bundle-archive-equivalence} gives the finite
4855: hash-and-manifest test, and every failed row of
4856: Table~\ref{tab:review-bundle-archive-equivalence} is a finite bad subrecord.  If
4857: all rows pass, the replacement denotes the same certificate bytes under the same
4858: relative paths and is normal form~(2); if any row fails, the archive cannot carry
4859: the bundle-backed claim.
4860: 
4861: Third, the candidate can point to a later or different workspace state.
4862: Theorem~\ref{thm:workspace-final-package-reconciliation} proves that such a state
4863: is not the old finite package unless it is deliberately promoted by fresh verifier
4864: runs and by a replacement commit--manifest certificate.
4865: Audit record~\ref{prop:mutable-checkout-observation-boundary} then shows that a
4866: bare mutable-checkout observation is non-certifying.  Therefore a different
4867: workspace is accepted only in normal form~(3), and otherwise has the finite
4868: command-boundary obstruction stated in the theorem.
4869: 
4870: The three cases are mutually exclusive as record modes for a fixed submitted
4871: claim: the first uses the selected directory, the second uses a byte-identical
4872: archive representative, and the third replaces the package state and digest
4873: record by a new common certificate.  If a proposed support reading is in none of
4874: the modes, it contributes no coordinate read by the verifier.  By
4875: Theorem~\ref{thm:finite-coordinate-determination-boundary} and the obstruction
4876: skeleton of Theorem~\ref{thm:finite-certificate-obstruction-skeleton}, the missing
4877: coordinate is an inclusion-minimal finite bad subrecord rather than a semantic
4878: fact about the underlying artifacts.\end{proof}
4879: 
4880: \begin{theorem}[Upload instantiation boundary]
4881: \label{thm:upload-or-archive-instantiation-boundary}
4882: Before the bundle-backed claims of this supplement are treated as part of a
4883: completed venue submission, the external submission record must instantiate the
4884: support-surface branch selected by
4885: Proposition~\ref{prop:final-package-shape-convention} and
4886: Theorems~\ref{thm:final-support-surface-closure} and
4887: \ref{thm:support-surface-normal-form}: it must record that
4888: \path{review_bundle/} was uploaded exactly with digest manifest $D_0$ and with
4889: the root \path{theorem_inventory.json} coordinate named by the manifest and
4890: ledger.  The TeX source and the local digest manifest select that exact-inclusion
4891: branch but do not constitute a venue upload receipt.  In the present source
4892: package no such external receipt is recorded; consequently all bundle-backed
4893: claims are proved only as conditional source-level support claims until the
4894: missing external exact-inclusion record is supplied.
4895: \end{theorem}
4896: 
4897: \begin{proof}
4898: Proposition~\ref{prop:final-package-shape-convention} and
4899: Theorem~\ref{thm:final-support-surface-closure} prove that the bundle-backed
4900: claims for this package are admissible in the exact-directory branch only.
4901: Audit record~\ref{prop:exact-review-bundle-upload-witness} and
4902: Audit record~\ref{prop:final-immutable-package-state-certificate} give the same
4903: selection and explicitly say that no archive locator is claimed.  Those source
4904: records determine what must be submitted, but they are produced before the
4905: venue's upload action and contain no venue receipt, DOI, institutional
4906: identifier, or external archive locator.  Hence a completed submission needs one
4907: additional external instantiation record: the venue or packager must record the
4908: exact supplemental directory upload with the final digest manifest.  Without that
4909: record, the statements proved above remain conditional source-level support
4910: claims rather than a proof that the upload action has occurred.  Therefore
4911: treating the bundle-backed claims as externally instantiated would add a
4912: coordinate not present in the finite support surface, contradicting the finite
4913: coordinate determination boundary of
4914: Theorem~\ref{thm:finite-coordinate-determination-boundary}.\end{proof}
4915: 
4916: \begin{corollary}[Upload-or-archive instantiation record]
4917: \label{cor:upload-or-archive-instantiation-record}
4918: The bundle-backed support claims of the current package may be used only under
4919: the external-record condition of
4920: Theorem~\ref{thm:upload-or-archive-instantiation-boundary}.  In particular,
4921: \path{review_bundle/FINAL_DIGESTS_SHA256.md} is a local byte-level packaging
4922: manifest and not, by itself, an upload receipt or an archive locator; no archive
4923: replacement branch is selected for this source package.
4924: \end{corollary}
4925: 
4926: \begin{proof}
4927: This is the record-level specialization of
4928: Theorem~\ref{thm:upload-or-archive-instantiation-boundary} to the current digest
4929: manifest.\end{proof}
4930: 
4931: \begin{proposition}[Upload-or-archive instantiation update protocol]
4932: \label{prop:upload-or-archive-instantiation-update-protocol}
4933: Suppose a later venue upload receipt or archive-equivalent locator is to be used
4934: to replace the current no-receipt boundary of
4935: Corollary~\ref{cor:upload-or-archive-instantiation-record} by an externally
4936: instantiated submitted-support claim.  Then the replacement is accepted by the
4937: finite-record interface if and only if one of the two following finite update
4938: protocols is performed.  The manuscript surfaces in the statement are precisely
4939: \path{submission_abstract.tex} and \path{main.tex}; the manifest surface is
4940: \path{review_bundle/REVIEW_BUNDLE_MANIFEST.json}; the bibliography surface is
4941: \path{references.bib}; and the digest surface is
4942: \path{review_bundle/FINAL_DIGESTS_SHA256.md} or a replacing digest manifest named
4943: by both manuscript sources and by the manifest.
4944: \begin{enumerate}
4945: \item \emph{Exact-upload update.}  \path{submission_abstract.tex} and
4946: \path{main.tex} record the receipt or venue
4947: submission identifier for the exact support surface selected in
4948: Proposition~\ref{prop:final-package-shape-convention}; the manifest field
4949: \path{public_interface.distribution_mode} is changed from conditional exact
4950: supplemental upload to completed exact supplemental upload; the manifest field
4951: \path{public_interface.preferred_submission_form} or an adjacent receipt field
4952: names the uploaded \path{submission_abstract.pdf}, \path{main.pdf} or
4953: \path{main.tex}, root \path{theorem_inventory.json}, and \path{review_bundle/};
4954: \path{review_bundle/FINAL_DIGESTS_SHA256.md} still contains matching digest rows
4955: for the submitted bundle files; and the \path{references.bib} note for
4956: \path{auditable-pipeline-review-bundle} is changed from no completed upload to the
4957: same receipt-bound support statement.
4958: \item \emph{Archive-equivalent update.}  \path{submission_abstract.tex} and
4959: \path{main.tex} record the archive
4960: locator; the manifest field \path{public_interface.current_public_archive} and the
4961: \path{references.bib} note for \path{auditable-pipeline-review-bundle} name that same
4962: locator; the manifest keeps or replaces \path{public_interface.archival_update_rule}
4963: with the byte-equivalence rule actually satisfied; and
4964: \path{review_bundle/FINAL_DIGESTS_SHA256.md}, or a replacing digest manifest named
4965: by both the manuscript and the manifest, records the file list and SHA--256 rows
4966: against which the archive is checked, including the coordinates for
4967: \path{review_bundle/}, \path{theorem_inventory.json}, and the manifest itself.
4968: \end{enumerate}
4969: In either protocol, if any digest row, manifest public-interface field,
4970: manuscript support statement, bibliography note, or receipt/locator coordinate is
4971: changed, all four surfaces must name the same support mode and the same finite
4972: receipt-or-locator record.  Without this finite common update, the current
4973: no-receipt normal form of
4974: Proposition~\ref{prop:submission-support-instantiation-field-normal-form} remains
4975: the only accepted submitted-support status.
4976: \end{proposition}
4977: 
4978: \begin{proof}
4979: The current package has only the source-level exact-inclusion branch by
4980: Proposition~\ref{prop:final-package-shape-convention} and
4981: Theorem~\ref{thm:upload-or-archive-instantiation-boundary}.  Thus an external
4982: instantiation can add exactly one new positive coordinate: either a receipt for
4983: that exact upload or a locator for an archive-equivalent representative.  The
4984: finite-coordinate determination boundary,
4985: Theorem~\ref{thm:finite-coordinate-determination-boundary}, forbids the verifier
4986: from reading any coordinate not present on the submitted support surface.  Hence
4987: the new coordinate must be visible wherever the package declares public support
4988: status: in the manuscript statement that changes the boundary, in the manifest
4989: public-interface fields that describe distribution mode and archive status, in
4990: the digest manifest that identifies the bytes being supplied, and in the
4991: bibliography entry that tells a reviewer whether the bundle is an external
4992: support surface or merely a local note.
4993: 
4994: For the exact-upload branch, the receipt is meaningful for this package only if
4995: it refers to the support surface selected by
4996: Proposition~\ref{prop:final-package-shape-convention}: the primary presentation
4997: artifact, the technical supplement, the root theorem inventory, and the exact
4998: \path{review_bundle/} directory with matching final digests.  Updating the
4999: manuscript, the manifest distribution fields, the digest record, and the
5000: bibliography note with the same receipt is therefore sufficient for the finite
5001: record checker to read the external-upload coordinate; if one of those records is
5002: missing or names a different support mode, the checker sees a bad subrecord of
5003: the kind classified by Theorem~\ref{thm:support-surface-normal-form}.
5004: 
5005: For the archive-equivalent branch, Table~\ref{tab:review-bundle-archive-equivalence}
5006: and Theorem~\ref{thm:support-surface-normal-form} require the archive to preserve
5007: the same file list, digest rows, manifest semantics, and relative-path meanings.
5008: The stated archive update records exactly those finite data: the common locator,
5009: the byte-equivalence rule, and the digest manifest identifying the archive bytes.
5010: Again, if the manuscript, manifest, bibliography, and digest surface do not name a
5011: single common locator and byte-equivalence certificate, the proposed archive is
5012: not a finite coordinate accepted by the verifier.
5013: 
5014: The two branches are exhaustive because
5015: Corollary~\ref{cor:upload-or-archive-instantiation-record} allows only an exact
5016: upload receipt or an archive-equivalent replacement to instantiate the support
5017: surface.  Therefore a future support claim is accepted exactly after one of the
5018: two finite common updates above, and otherwise the no-receipt normal form remains
5019: the accepted status.
5020: \end{proof}
5021: 
5022: \begin{corollary}[Current no-receipt support-surface non-escalation]
5023: \label{cor:current-no-receipt-support-surface-non-escalation}
5024: In the current source package the records
5025: \path{review_bundle/FINAL_DIGESTS_SHA256.md},
5026: \path{review_bundle/REVIEW_BUNDLE_MANIFEST.json},
5027: \path{review_bundle/current_package_pass_records.json}, and
5028: \path{theorem_inventory.json} do not contain a venue upload receipt, public DOI,
5029: institutional archive identifier, or archive-equivalent locator for
5030: \path{review_bundle/}.  Hence every claim whose evidence surface is a
5031: bundle-local path is accepted only as a conditional exact-supplemental-inclusion
5032: claim.  Such a claim becomes an externally instantiated submitted-support claim
5033: only after one of the two finite records below is added to the submitted support
5034: surface:
5035: \begin{enumerate}
5036: \item an upload receipt naming the exact \path{review_bundle/} directory and the
5037: final digest manifest; or
5038: \item an archive-equivalent locator satisfying the file-list, digest, manifest,
5039: and path-semantics tests of
5040: Audit record~\ref{audit:review-bundle-archive-equivalence}.
5041: \end{enumerate}
5042: Until then, the theorem inventory, verifier logs, case snapshots, source
5043: snapshot, and primary-claim inventory remain local/path-verified review-bundle
5044: coordinates rather than unconditional public or venue-submitted coordinates.
5045: \end{corollary}
5046: 
5047: \begin{proof}
5048: The four named files are the only finite records in the present source package
5049: that select the support branch for \path{review_bundle/}: the digest manifest
5050: gives the byte-level package identity, the review-bundle manifest gives the
5051: submission strategy, the pass-record ledger exposes the accepted finite gates,
5052: and \path{theorem_inventory.json} is the manual theorem-ledger coordinate.  Their
5053: recorded branch is exact supplemental inclusion and their archive fields state
5054: that no archive replacement or locator is claimed.  Therefore they determine the
5055: bytes and paths that must be supplied, but they do not determine that a venue
5056: upload, DOI minting event, institutional archiving event, or archive-equivalent
5057: publication event has occurred.
5058: 
5059: By Theorem~\ref{thm:upload-or-archive-instantiation-boundary}, an externally
5060: instantiated bundle-backed claim needs exactly the missing external coordinate:
5061: either an upload record for the exact directory and final digest manifest, or a
5062: replacement archive record passing
5063: Audit record~\ref{audit:review-bundle-archive-equivalence}.  By
5064: Corollary~\ref{cor:upload-or-archive-instantiation-record}, the digest manifest
5065: alone is not such a coordinate.  If neither finite record is present, promoting a
5066: bundle-local path to an unconditional submitted-support coordinate would add an
5067: evidence coordinate not contained in the support surface, contrary to
5068: Theorem~\ref{thm:finite-coordinate-determination-boundary}.  The stated
5069: conditional boundary follows for every bundle-backed surface named in the
5070: corollary.
5071: \end{proof}
5072: 
5073: \begin{corollary}[Fresh inventory digest instance for this source state]
5074: \label{cor:fresh-inventory-digest-instance-this-source-state}
5075: In the present Stage-A source state, the regenerated files
5076: \path{theorem_inventory.json} and \path{theorem_inventory.md} are closed as local
5077: exact-inclusion coordinates only after their SHA-256 rows in
5078: \path{review_bundle/FINAL_DIGESTS_SHA256.md} are recomputed from the bytes of
5079: those two files and the finite command-boundary table names that refreshed
5080: manifest state.  This corollary supplies no upload receipt, archive locator,
5081: extractor-completeness certificate, or semantic proof check; it supplies only the
5082: local byte-coordinate instance required by
5083: Corollary~\ref{cor:current-theorem-inventory-digest-instance}.
5084: \end{corollary}
5085: 
5086: \begin{proof}
5087: There are two relevant file coordinates, namely
5088: \path{theorem_inventory.json} and \path{theorem_inventory.md}.  For each
5089: coordinate the SHA-256 computation is a deterministic function of the finite byte
5090: string stored at that relative path.  Replacing the rows in
5091: \path{review_bundle/FINAL_DIGESTS_SHA256.md} by the values computed after the
5092: Stage-A regeneration therefore makes the digest manifest name the regenerated
5093: bytes rather than a prior or anticipated inventory state.  The command-boundary
5094: table is the only place in the manuscript where command-run and freshness claims
5095: are promoted beyond path names, so updating that table to the same refreshed
5096: state prevents a stale 2026-06-05 package description from being read as the
5097: current digest instance.  The argument uses only byte equality at the two named
5098: paths and the finite-record boundary of
5099: Theorem~\ref{thm:digest-closure-refresh-criterion}; it does not add an extractor
5100: run, external support-surface instantiation, upload event, archive event, or
5101: semantic validation.  Hence exactly the local digest-closure claim stated above
5102: is obtained.
5103: \end{proof}
5104: 
5105: \begin{theorem}[Digest-closure refresh criterion for final package claims]
5106: \label{thm:digest-closure-refresh-criterion}
5107: For the current presentation package, any claim that a submitted support surface
5108: has exact final digests is accepted only for a closed finite state $D$ satisfying
5109: all of the following conditions.
5110: \begin{enumerate}
5111: \item The digest manifest \path{review_bundle/FINAL_DIGESTS_SHA256.md} contains
5112: SHA-256 rows for \path{main.tex}, \path{submission_abstract.tex},
5113: \path{references.bib}, \path{source_interface_record.json},
5114: \path{theorem_inventory.json}, \path{theorem_inventory.md}, and every file in
5115: the selected \path{review_bundle/} support directory.
5116: \item The digest rows are computed after the accepted versions of
5117: \path{theorem_inventory.json}, \path{theorem_inventory.md},
5118: \path{review_bundle/primary_claim_inventory.json}, and every verifier log named
5119: by a command-run claim have been written.
5120: \item If \path{submission_abstract.tex} is edited after the primary-claim
5121: inventory was checked, then
5122: \path{review_bundle/verify_primary_claim_inventory.py} is rerun and its fresh
5123: log replaces the old primary-inventory freshness coordinate before the final
5124: digest rows are recomputed.
5125: \item If an upload-time venue-compliance claim, rather than a dated local
5126: readiness observation, is made, the venue and bibliography check is rerun at the
5127: upload rule state and the fresh venue record is included before the final digest
5128: rows are recomputed.
5129: \end{enumerate}
5130: If any one of these conditions fails, the package still has the local
5131: path-verified records printed in the manuscript, but it does not have an exact
5132: final-digest certificate for the regenerated inventory, primary-claim, or
5133: upload-time venue component that failed the condition.
5134: \end{theorem}
5135: 
5136: \begin{proof}
5137: The support-surface certificate is byte-level: by
5138: Theorem~\ref{thm:support-surface-normal-form}, exact inclusion and
5139: archive-equivalent inclusion both read the finite file list, relative paths, and
5140: SHA-256 content rows rather than prose descriptions of those files.  Therefore a
5141: file written after the digest manifest was computed cannot be covered by that
5142: manifest; its byte string was not one of the inputs to the listed hash values.
5143: This proves the necessity of recomputing the digest rows after regenerating the
5144: theorem inventory, primary-claim inventory, and command logs named by the final
5145: package.
5146: 
5147: The primary-claim inventory is line-span dependent.  Its verifier reads the
5148: current \path{submission_abstract.tex}, checks the row-id set and line ranges,
5149: and prints a finite freshness log.  If the primary source is changed after that
5150: run, at least the source line-span premise of the old log is no longer the
5151: current primary source checked by the verifier.  A fresh verifier run before the
5152: digest pass restores a finite coordinate for the new primary state; omitting it
5153: leaves only the old path-verified inventory observation.
5154: 
5155: Venue compliance is external-state dependent by
5156: Proposition~\ref{audit:fresh-venue-record-criterion} and
5157: Theorem~\ref{thm:venue-rule-freshness-non-escalation}.  A dated venue log can
5158: witness local readiness at its observation time, but upload-time compliance
5159: requires a record of the rule state at upload or an included replacement record.
5160: Thus a package that claims upload-time venue compliance must write that fresh
5161: record before the digest closure step; otherwise the digest manifest can cover
5162: only the dated local-readiness file, not the missing upload-time premise.
5163: 
5164: Combining these observations gives a finite fixed-point condition: first write
5165: the accepted inventory files and freshness logs, then compute the manifest over
5166: those bytes, and finally submit either the exact directory or an
5167: archive-equivalent replacement.  If a later edit or upload-time claim changes one
5168: of the inputs, the fixed point is broken precisely at that finite subrecord.  The
5169: remaining local rows remain available at their declared evidence levels, but the
5170: stronger exact final-digest claim is not accepted for the changed component.
5171: \end{proof}
5172: 
5173: 
5174: \begin{proposition}[Primary architectural fallback without external support]
5175: \label{prop:primary-architectural-fallback-without-external-support}
5176: Assume the current source package is used without an upload receipt for the exact
5177: \path{review_bundle/} directory and without an archive-equivalent replacement
5178: satisfying Audit record~\ref{audit:review-bundle-archive-equivalence}.  Then the
5179: primary presentation article may assert only the source-level architecture and
5180: path-verified local-package claims whose evidence surfaces are visible outside the
5181: missing bundle.  In particular, the theorem-ledger claim of
5182: Theorem~\ref{thm:theorem-obligation-ledger-boundary}, the case-snapshot claims,
5183: the verifier-log claims, and any claim whose certificate coordinate is
5184: \path{theorem_inventory.json} or a file under \path{review_bundle/} cannot be
5185: read as externally submitted evidence.  If either accepted external instantiation
5186: record is later supplied, the same claims re-enter exactly at the finite evidence
5187: level stated in their certificate rows and not at any stronger semantic or venue
5188: acceptance level.
5189: \end{proposition}
5190: 
5191: \begin{proof}
5192: Corollary~\ref{cor:current-no-receipt-support-surface-non-escalation} identifies
5193: the only two records that can externally instantiate a bundle-backed support
5194: claim: an exact upload receipt for \path{review_bundle/} with the final digest
5195: manifest, or an archive-equivalent locator passing the finite file-list, digest,
5196: manifest, and path-semantics tests.  Under the present hypothesis neither record
5197: is available.  Hence every bundle-local path is absent from the externally
5198: submitted finite support surface.
5199: 
5200: The affected claims are precisely those whose certificate coordinate names such a
5201: path.  Table~\ref{tab:submitted-theorem-obligation-ledger} places the manual
5202: theorem inventory at \path{theorem_inventory.json} and exposes it through
5203: \path{review_bundle/current_package_pass_records.json}; the case-snapshot and
5204: verifier-log statements similarly name files under \path{review_bundle/}.  By
5205: Theorem~\ref{thm:finite-coordinate-determination-boundary}, a claim cannot acquire
5206: an evidence coordinate that is absent from the finite support surface.  Therefore
5207: those claims cannot be read as externally submitted evidence while both accepted
5208: instantiation records are missing.
5209: 
5210: Removing that external reading does not remove the primary article's independent
5211: architectural assertion.  The primary text describes the compiler's typed record
5212: interface and cites the pinned public source surface; those claims do not require
5213: the missing bundle-local coordinate.  If a valid exact-upload or
5214: archive-equivalent record is later supplied, Theorem~\ref{thm:support-surface-normal-form}
5215: and Corollary~\ref{cor:upload-or-archive-instantiation-record} put the
5216: bundle-backed claims back into the finite support surface.  The reinstatement is
5217: only at the recorded evidence levels, because the same corollaries and
5218: Theorem~\ref{thm:upload-or-archive-instantiation-boundary} exclude stronger
5219: readings such as semantic proof checking, fresh dynamic validation, venue
5220: compliance, or acceptance.\end{proof}
