5436: \begin{theorem}[Seven-row submitted theorem-obligation ledger integration]
5437: \label{thm:theorem-obligation-ledger-boundary}
5438: Let $P^{+}_{7}$ be the seven-row support state obtained from $P^{+}_{6}$
5439: by the conservative finite-record extension of
5440: Theorem~\ref{thm:nested-package-states}, namely by adding exactly the manual
5441: submitted theorem-ledger coordinate \path{a7}.  In
5442: $P^{+}_{7}$, the theorem-obligation ledger is no longer a detached review-only
5443: artifact: the submitted finite support surface contains
5444: \path{theorem_inventory.json} through the manifest field \path{theorem_inventory}
5445: and through acceptance-ledger entry \path{a7}.  The earlier six-row state
5446: $P^{+}_{6}$ of Theorems~\ref{thm:nested-package-states}
5447: and~\ref{thm:current-package-certificate-exactness} remains
5448: the row-frozen certificate state for \path{a1}--\path{a6}; the present theorem
5449: adds exactly the manual theorem-ledger coordinate \path{a7}.  Consequently the
5450: package may make
5451: the following bounded theorem-ledger claim: every theorem-obligation assertion
5452: made by the submission is supported only through the finite coordinates in
5453: Table~\ref{tab:submitted-theorem-obligation-ledger}, namely the integrated
5454: theorem inventory, the primary-claim inventory, the certificate ledger, and the
5455: manifest exposure records.  By
5456: Proposition~\ref{prop:manual-theorem-inventory-boundary}, this is a manual
5457: Stage-A obligation ledger claim, not a deterministic theorem-environment
5458: extraction or completeness claim.  The claim does not assert that
5459: \path{theorem_inventory.json} proves the mathematical semantics of each theorem,
5460: does not replace the proofs printed in this source, and does not certify a Lean
5461: rebuild, publication-daemon run, Rule110 artifact rerun, extractor run, or
5462: external upload.
5463: \end{theorem}
5464: 
5465: \begin{proof}
5466: The support surface is finite and can be inspected coordinate by coordinate.
5467: The root manifest now contains the key \path{theorem_inventory} with value
5468: \path{theorem_inventory.json}.  The certificate schema includes the same key in
5469: its required manifest-file map.  Therefore a certificate-record verification of
5470: the enlarged package must check that the manifest exposes this root-level
5471: inventory path and that the file is present.  This removes the previous
5472: possibility of silently citing a root-level Stage-A artifact outside the support
5473: surface.
5474: 
5475: The acceptance ledger contains the additional entry \path{a7}.  Its accepted
5476: claim is exactly the bounded submitted theorem-obligation ledger claim; its
5477: claim kinds are \path{traceability} and \path{submission}.  Under the schema's
5478: gate dispatch, those kinds require the inventory, marker-existence, and
5479: submission-pack gates.  Entry \path{a7} supplies precisely those three pass
5480: records: the inventory gate points to \path{theorem_inventory.json}, the
5481: marker-existence gate points to
5482: Table~\ref{tab:submitted-theorem-obligation-ledger}, and the submission-pack
5483: gate points to \path{review_bundle/REVIEW_BUNDLE_MANIFEST.json}.  Thus the
5484: ledger supplies a finite route from the theorem-inventory file to the submitted
5485: certificate records rather than a prose-only reference.
5486: 
5487: It remains to identify the boundary.  The schema-level verifier checks finite
5488: record shape, required manifest paths, gate coverage, evidence pointers, and
5489: evidence levels.  None of those checks is a semantic proof of the theorem-like
5490: environments in this source, and none reruns Lean, the publication daemon, the
5491: Rule110/GroundCompiler artifacts, or an independent theorem-environment
5492: extractor.  Proposition~\ref{prop:manual-theorem-inventory-boundary} supplies the
5493: missing classification: the inventory is an accepted manual Stage-A ledger and
5494: not an executable completeness certificate.  The theorem-ledger claim is
5495: therefore admissible only at the path-verified evidence level stated in
5496: \path{a7}.  The mathematical content of the article remains carried by the
5497: printed definitions, propositions, lemmas, theorems, and proofs, and external
5498: records carry only the finite evidence claims that cite them.  The integrated
5499: inventory gives the submitted finite obligation surface against which those
5500: theorem-like claims are enumerated; it indexes the obligations and does not prove
5501: them.  This is exactly the bounded claim stated in the theorem.
5502: \end{proof}
