5504: \begin{proposition}[Submitted theorem-inventory availability]
5505: \label{prop:submitted-theorem-inventory-availability}
5506: If the external support-surface condition of
5507: Corollary~\ref{cor:upload-or-archive-instantiation-record} is satisfied, then
5508: \path{theorem_inventory.json} is an available submitted certificate coordinate
5509: for the bounded manual theorem-obligation ledger claim of
5510: Theorem~\ref{thm:theorem-obligation-ledger-boundary}.  If the exact bundle is not
5511: uploaded with matching final digests, the theorem inventory has only local
5512: diagnostic force and cannot support a submitted theorem-ledger claim in the
5513: current package.
5514: \end{proposition}
5515: 
5516: \begin{proof}
5517: The first sentence is the exact-bundle branch of
5518: Theorem~\ref{thm:final-support-surface-closure} applied to the manifest-exposed
5519: coordinate \path{theorem_inventory.json} and the ledger-exposed coordinate
5520: \path{a7}.  In that branch, the file named by the manifest is available to the
5521: reviewer as part of the submitted finite support surface, so it may be used for
5522: the bounded theorem-ledger claim.  If the exact bundle is not supplied with
5523: matching final digests, Corollary~\ref{cor:upload-or-archive-instantiation-record}
5524: prevents all bundle-backed support claims from being externally instantiated for
5525: this package.  The theorem inventory then remains a local file rather than a
5526: submitted support coordinate, so it cannot carry the submitted theorem-ledger
5527: claim.
5528: \end{proof}
