5549: this package only as a no-receipt, no-archive boundary record.  This normal form
5550: does not satisfy the external submitted-support branch; it proves instead that
5551: bundle-backed claims may be read only as conditional local package-support
5552: claims until a later upload receipt or archive-equivalent locator is added by the
5553: finite update protocol of
5554: Proposition~\ref{prop:upload-or-archive-instantiation-update-protocol}.
5555: \end{proposition}
5556: 
5557: \begin{proof}
5558: The support branch is fixed by
5559: Proposition~\ref{prop:final-package-shape-convention}: the selected supplement is
5560: \path{main.tex}, the selected theorem ledger is \path{theorem_inventory.json},
5561: and the selected review surface is exact inclusion of \path{review_bundle/} with
5562: \path{review_bundle/FINAL_DIGESTS_SHA256.md}.  Theorem~\ref{thm:upload-or-archive-instantiation-boundary}
5563: then identifies the extra coordinate needed to turn that local support surface
5564: into an externally submitted one, namely either an exact upload receipt or an
5565: archive-equivalent locator.  Corollary~\ref{cor:current-no-receipt-support-surface-non-escalation}
5566: records that neither coordinate is present in the current source package.  These
5567: three finite statements determine all four fields in the displayed table, while
5568: Proposition~\ref{prop:upload-or-archive-instantiation-update-protocol} specifies
5569: the finite manuscript, manifest, bibliography, and digest updates needed to leave
5570: this normal form in a later package.
