5581: \begin{proposition}[Review-bundle availability condition]
5582: \label{audit:review-bundle-availability-condition}
5583: The final support mode selected for the current presentation package is exact
5584: supplemental inclusion of \path{review_bundle/}, conditional on the external
5585: instantiation record of Corollary~\ref{cor:upload-or-archive-instantiation-record}, as recorded in
5586: \path{review_bundle/FINAL_DIGESTS_SHA256.md} and in
5587: Audit record~\ref{prop:final-immutable-package-state-certificate}.  This is a
5588: conditional support-mode selection, not a completed venue-upload record or public
5589: archive locator.  The source-interface, case-snapshot, primary-claim inventory,
5590: submission-interface map, theorem-inventory, and verifier-record claims are
5591: therefore reviewable at the path-verified evidence level stated in this
5592: supplement only under the exact included bundle once the external instantiation
5593: record exists.  A future archival equivalent would have to satisfy
5594: Audit record~\ref{audit:review-bundle-archive-equivalence} and the common-field
5595: update protocol of
5596: Proposition~\ref{prop:upload-or-archive-instantiation-update-protocol}, but it is
5597: not the current package branch.  If the bundle is not uploaded exactly with matching
5598: final digests, then the primary note retains only the public-source citation to
5599: the pinned newmath repository and the architectural claim in the short text; the
5600: supplemental support claims depending on bundle-local files are not accepted by
5601: this package.
5602: \end{proposition}
5603: 
5604: 
5605: \medskip
5606: \begin{proof}
5607: The bundle-dependent support claims are exactly the claims whose certificate
5608: surface names files under \path{review_bundle/}.  Proposition~\ref{prop:machine-readable-certificate-records}
5609: lists the schema, current pass-record ledger, submission-interface map,
5610: primary-claim inventory, verifier script, and verifier log as bundle files.
5611: Proposition~\ref{prop:reviewable-source-snapshot-interface} uses the bundled
5612: source snapshot, and Proposition~\ref{prop:review-bundle-case-snapshot-coverage}
5613: uses the bundled case snapshots.  Therefore, when \path{review_bundle/} is
5614: actually included as exact supplemental material with matching final digests,
5615: each such certificate surface lies in the submitted artifact boundary and is
5616: locally checkable in the sense of the finite schema verifier.  Until the external
5617: upload record specified in
5618: Corollary~\ref{cor:upload-or-archive-instantiation-record} exists, these
5619: bundle-backed statements are conditional support claims rather than independent
5620: public-access claims.
5621: 
5622: If the bundle is absent, those bundle-local paths are no longer in the submitted
5623: artifact boundary.  The definition of local checkability requires every named
5624: path, manifest row, or log to lie in the submitted artifact, the supplemental
5625: review bundle, or an explicit path-verified historical boundary.  No DOI or
5626: institutional archive identifier is claimed in this package, so an omitted bundle
5627: has no replacement surface unless an archival equivalent satisfying
5628: Audit record~\ref{audit:review-bundle-archive-equivalence} is provided.  If neither
5629: surface is present, the affected claims fail the evidence-surface check of
5630: Proposition~\ref{prop:finite-certificate-schema-verifier}.  What remains is only
5631: the public repository citation at the pinned commit and the short note's
5632: architectural thesis, not the bundle-backed support certification.
5633: \end{proof}
5634: 
5635: \begin{proposition}[Case-snapshot non-rerun boundary]
5636: \label{audit:case-snapshot-non-rerun-boundary}
5637: Under the hypotheses of
5638: Propositions~\ref{prop:path-complete-case-witnesses} and
5639: \ref{prop:review-bundle-case-snapshot-coverage}, the four case-study rows cannot
5640: be read as fresh dynamic-behavior claims.  Any stronger reading asserting a fresh
5641: publication-daemon execution, full-source rebuild, theorem-content rerun,
5642: Rule110 dynamic rerun, or GroundCompiler semantic rerun requires command, source
5643: state, environment, exit-code, and log-path fields in addition to the bundled
5644: snapshots.  Without those fields the stronger reading is rejected by the finite
5645: record verifier at its evidence-strength boundary.
5646: \end{proposition}
5647: 
5648: 
5649: \medskip
5650: \begin{proof}
5651: The propositions identify the complete evidence surface of the case rows:
5652: thirteen local-path strings, thirteen reviewable bundle snapshots, and manifest
5653: boundaries recording historical or path-verified evidence.  None of those case
5654: rows contains the five command-run fields required by
5655: Definition~\ref{def:operational-acceptance-interface}.  A fresh daemon,
5656: full-source, theorem-content, Rule110, or GroundCompiler rerun is therefore a
5657: strictly stronger evidence-level assertion than the accepted row supplies.  By
5658: Proposition~\ref{prop:finite-certificate-schema-verifier} and
5659: the schema-relative finite-record exactness theorem, Theorem~\ref{thm:record-acceptance-exactness}, the same certificate cannot accept
5660: that stronger assertion: its boundary field $B$ records no command-run assertion,
5661: and the missing command tuple is a finite bad subrecord.  Thus the snapshots are
5662: rigidly limited to path-verified reviewability unless a separate rerun log is
5663: added.
5664: \end{proof}
